        "original_id": "109c0709-7f00-537c-9f99-b81584ceb2b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Glazunov\n- Works: Symphony No. 9 in D minor\n- Organizations: Saint Petersburg Conservatory, Petrograd Conservatory, Leningrad Conservatory\n- Events: Bolshevik Revolution\n- Roles: Director\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander Glazunov began composing Symphony No. 9 in D minor in 1910.\n- Alexander Glazunov served as director of the Saint Petersburg Conservatory from 1905 to 1928.\n- Following the Bolshevik Revolution, Alexander Glazunov helped reorganize the Saint Petersburg Conservatory into the Petrograd Conservatory and later the Leningrad Conservatory.\n- Symphony No. 9 in D minor remained unfinished when Alexander Glazunov died in 1936.",
